    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0632" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v19/pg606"/>

                <head>302. Telegram From the Embassy in Iran to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d302-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Tehran</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-05-28T15:00:00+03:30">May 28, 1963, 3
                            p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1038. I concluded telecon with Steeves ten
                    minutes ago in which he reported that after two and a half-hours with Afghan
                        King,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d302-f2"/> he was unable to move him beyond
                    agreement to give Paks confidential assurance of
                    good behavior with Afghan wording reported in Embtel 1035<anchor n="2" xml:id="d302-f3"/> “each side would
                    endeavor to bring about an atmosphere of good understanding, friendship and
                    mutual trust” or to delete all reference to the matter in the communique.</p>
                <p>On telephoning Foreign Minister for appointment to convey our latest information,
                    he told me that a few minutes earlier agreement had been reached as result of
                    another concession by Paks to accept
                    confidential assurance of good behavior.</p>
                <p>There will be a joint meeting at five o’clock local time to finalize agreed text
                    of communique which will not be made public before tomorrow. Aram elated and asked me to celebration dinner
                    this evening.</p>
                <p>I recommend immediate dispatch messages of congratulations on successful outcome
                    from President to Shah and from Secretary
                    to Aram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Holmes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d302-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d302-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, POL
                        AFG-PAK. Confidential; Operational
                    Immediate. Repeated to Kabul and Karachi.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d302-f2" n="1" xml:id="d302-f2-content">
                <p>Steeves reported on his conversation with
                    King Zahir on May 28 in airgram A-522
                    from Kabul, June 2. (Ibid., POL 32-1 AFG-PAK)</p>
            </note>
